# The whole-tree golangci-lint finding ceiling.
#
# One number: how many findings `golangci-lint run` over the whole tree is
# allowed to report. scripts/lint-ceiling.sh compares the measured count against
# it, and `make full` fails when the count is higher.
#
# THE NUMBER ONLY GOES DOWN. A run that comes in under the ceiling rewrites this
# file to the lower count, so the ground a fix wins is never given back. Commit
# the change with the fix.
#
# Raising it is the one repair that is not allowed. If a change adds findings,
# fix the findings. Run `.tools/golangci-lint run --new-from-rev=HEAD~1` to see
# only the ones you added — that is the same check `make fast` runs.
#
# Everything below the comments is one line holding one whole number. Anything
# else fails the build rather than defaulting, because every default here is a
# number that lets a commit through.
1184
